k competitor"},{"name":"dYdX Chain","relationship":"exchange-appchain competitor"},{"name":"Avalanche C-Chain DEXs","relationship":"shared-chain liquidity competitors"}],"narrative_arc":"Dexalot moved from C-Chain contracts to a purpose-built Avalanche L1, then expanded the same order book toward multi-chain asset access.","media_sentiment":"mixed"},"risk":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","exploits":[],"sanctions":{"flagged":false,"detail":"No base-chain designation is recorded here; markets, interfaces, assets, and addresses require separate screening."},"extraction_flags":["validator_concentration","bridge_dependency","orderbook_liquidity_concentration"],"audit_status":"Dexalot reports audited contracts and security practices; this dossier did not independently reconcile every deployed version to every audit.","risks":[{"type":"bridge_and_message_risk","detail":"Deposits and withdrawals cross chain boundaries, so messaging or bridge failures can strand access."},{"type":"thin_security_budget","detail":"A low token market capitalization can weaken validator economics and appchain security."},{"type":"liquidity_quality","detail":"High reported volume relative to TVL requires scrutiny of market depth, makers, and wash-trading resistance."}]},"synthesis":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","situation":"Dexalot reports about $26.2 million daily spot volume against only $1.46 million TVL and an ALOT market cap below $1 million; the exchange remains active but the security and liquidity ratios warrant scrutiny.","postmortem":null,"why":"The dedicated appchain gives an order book predictable execution and avoids shared-chain congestion. The model succeeds only if cross-chain access, validator security, and professional market-maker liquidity remain coordinated.","strategic_choices":[{"decision":"Move order execution from C-Chain to a dedicated Avalanche L1.","consequence":"Performance and fee control improved while bridge and validator dependencies increased.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://docs.dexalot.com/en/articles/subnet/"]},{"decision":"Retain non-custodial onchain order books instead of an offchain matcher.","consequence":"Auditability improves, with higher infrastructure complexity than a hybrid exchange.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://dexalot.com/en/about"]},{"decision":"Expand deposits across chains while centralizing execution liquidity.","consequence":"One book can aggregate users, but messaging failures become a systemic boundary.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["https://dexalot.com/en/about","https://dexalot.com/docs/DEXALOT-Litepaper.pdf"]}],"lessons_learned":["An appchain can optimize exchange execution but inherits its own security budget.","Volume-to-TVL ratios need market-quality context.","Cross-chain user reach and execution centralization create correlated bridge risk."],"could_differ":"Remaining solely on Avalanche C-Chain would have reduced bridge and validator complexity but exposed matching to shared congestion and less predictable fees.","unknowns":["How concentrated is validator voting power?","What share of volume is attributable to a small number of market makers?","What current bridge limits and emergency controls exist?","What is the complete financing and treasury position?"],"outlook":{"bull":"Omni-chain deposits deepen a single transparent order book.","base":"Dexalot remains a niche exchange appchain with active volume but thin token security.","bear":"Bridge failure, maker exit, or weak validator economics undermines the book.","most_likely":"base"},"cause_tags":["exchange_appchain","central_limit_order_book","cross_chain_distribution","thin_security_budget"],"confidence":"medium"}},"meta":{"dimension_completeness_pct":100,"data_completeness_pct":75,"confidence":"medium","unsourced_fields":["team.founders","capital.total_raised_usd","capital.treasury_usd","onchain.stablecoin_tvl_usd","onchain.revenue_30d_usd","onchain.active_addresses_daily","onchain.dev_activity_monthly","onchain.tvl_concentration"],"last_reviewed":"2026-07-29"}},{"chain":"Thorchain","source_catalog":{"launch":{"title":"THORChain Multichain Chaosnet launch","url":"https://blog.thorchain.org/weekly-dev-update-89"},"v3":{"title":"THORChain V3 release","url":"https://blog.thorchain.org/thorchain-v3-release"},"rune":{"title":"RUNE roles and economic security","url":"https://docs.thorchain.org/technical-documentation/understanding-thorchain/rune"},"security":{"title":"THORChain network security and governance","url":"https://docs.thorchain.org/network-security-governance"},"unwind":{"title":"THORFi unwind","url":"https://blog.thorchain.org/thorfi-unwind"},"tokenomics":{"title":"RUNE and TCY tokenomics","url":"https://docs.thorchain.org/tokenomics-rune-tcy"},"token":{"title":"CoinGecko THORChain market data API","url":"https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/thorchain"},"tvl":{"title":"DefiLlama Thorchain historical TVL API","url":"https://api.llama.fi/v2/historicalChainTvl/Thorchain"},"fees":{"title":"DefiLlama Thorchain fees API","url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/fees/Thorchain?dataType=dailyFees"},"volume":{"title":"DefiLlama Thorchain DEX volume API","url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/dexs/Thorchain?dataType=dailyVolume"},"ofac":{"title":"OFAC sanctions list data formats","url":"https://ofac.treasury.gov/specially-designated-nationals-list-data-formats-data-schemas"}},"dimension_sources":{"identity":["launch","v3","unwind"],"token":["rune","tokenomics","token"],"capital":["tokenomics"],"onchain":["tvl","fees","volume"],"team":["launch","security","unwind"],"narrative":["v3","rune","tokenomics"],"risk":["security","unwind","tokenomics","ofac"],"synthesis":["v3","rune","security","unwind","tokenomics","tvl","fees","volume"]},"dimensions":{"identity":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","chain":"Thorchain","aliases":["THORChain","MCCN"],"category":"L1","vm":"CosmWasm","launched":"2021-04-13","status":"recovering","lifecycle":[{"date":"2021-04-13","type":"launch","description":"Multichain Chaosnet launched with capped native-asset liquidity.","source_url":"https://blog.thorchain.org/weekly-dev-update-89"},{"date":"2024-12-21","type":"v3_upgrade","description":"THORChain V3 added an application-layer path and broader protocol capabilities.","source_url":"https://blog.thorchain.org/thorchain-v3-release"},{"date":"2025-01-24","type":"economic_restructuring","description":"Nodes paused Lending and Savers amid roughly $206 million of THORFi liabilities; the unwind later converted creditor claims into TCY.","source_url":"https://blog.thorchain.org/thorfi-unwind"}]},"token":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","launch_status":"launched","token_symbol":"RUNE","gas_token":"RUNE","launch_date":"2019","launch_date_precision":"year","launch_relation":"RUNE predates MCCN and is the settlement, bond, fee, governance-signaling, and incentive asset.","token_cg_id":"thorchain","token_current_usd":0.432561,"token_ath_usd":20.87,"token_ath_date":"2021-05-18","price_drawdown_pct":97.93,"market_cap_usd":146309367,"fdv_usd":153191438,"circulating_supply":338181666,"total_supply":354088937,"max_supply":354088937,"unlock_overhang_pct":4.49,"economic_design":"RUNE pairs against pooled assets and bonds validators; after the THORFi unwind, TCY represents creditor claims and receives a documented share of network revenue.","source_url":"https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/thorchain"},"capital":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","total_raised_usd":null,"rounds":[],"treasury_usd":null,"backers_tier":"mixed","notes":"Genesis allocation documents seed and IDO percentages but this dossier does not convert token allocations into an unreconciled USD financing total."},"onchain":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","tvl_peak_usd":546437336,"tvl_peak_date":"2022-04-02","tvl_current_usd":28752461,"tvl_drawdown_pct":94.74,"stablecoin_tvl_usd":null,"spot_dex_volume_24h_usd":12593502,"spot_dex_volume_30d_usd":737486475,"fees_24h_usd":316,"fees_30d_usd":202414,"revenue_30d_usd":null,"active_addresses_daily":null,"dev_activity_monthly":null,"tvl_concentration":null,"source_url":"https://api.llama.fi/v2/historicalChainTvl/Thorchain","fees_source_url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/fees/Thorchain?dataType=dailyFees","volume_source_url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/dexs/Thorchain?dataType=dailyVolume"},"team":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","founders":[],"entity":"Pseudonymous-origin open-source protocol; active THORNode operators govern operational and economic parameters through Mimir","key_events":[{"date":"2021-04-13","type":"launch","description":"Multichain Chaosnet launched.","source_url":"https://blog.thorchain.org/weekly-dev-update-89"},{"date":"2025-01-24","type":"governance","description":"Node votes paused THORFi after liabilities and RUNE reflexivity threatened network stability.","source_url":"https://blog.thorchain.org/thorfi-unwind"}],"regulatory_status":"Permissionless cross-chain swaps can attract sanctions, money-transmission, exchange, and interface scrutiny; no universal legal classification is asserted."},"narrative":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","purpose":"Native-asset cross-chain swaps without centralized custody or wrapped-asset settlement.","positioning":"A threshold-signed liquidity and settlement network where RUNE economically secures native assets across chains.","competitors":[{"name":"Centralized exchanges","relationship":"native cross-chain conversion incumbents"},{"name":"LayerZero and bridge aggregators","relationship":"cross-chain movement alternatives"},{"name":"Maya Protocol","relationship":"THORChain-derived native-swap competitor"}],"narrative_arc":"THORChain pioneered native cross-chain liquidity, survived early security incidents, expanded into THORFi, then unwound roughly $206 million of liabilities and refocused on swaps and an application layer.","media_sentiment":"mixed"},"risk":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","exploits":[{"date":"2025-01-24","amount_usd":206000000,"type":"economic insolvency and liability restructuring","description":"THORFi Savers, Lending, and unattached synth liabilities were approximately $206 million when nodes paused the products; this is not classified as a code theft.","source_url":"https://blog.thorchain.org/thorfi-unwind"}],"sanctions":{"flagged":false,"detail":"No base-chain designation is recorded here; cross-chain vaults, addresses, interfaces, and flows require separate screening."},"extraction_flags":["tss_vault_risk","rune_reflexivity","validator_concentration","cross_chain_attack_surface"],"audit_status":"Open-source code and multiple security mechanisms exist; each connected chain, vault implementation, and application-layer module creates a separate review surface.","risks":[{"type":"economic_reflexivity","detail":"RUNE simultaneously secures, settles, and capitalizes liquidity, so price declines can weaken multiple safeguards together."},{"type":"threshold_vault","detail":"Native assets sit in threshold-signed vaults whose safety depends on node diversity, churn, and implementation correctness."},{"type":"product_scope","detail":"The THORFi failure shows that adding credit and synthetic leverage can create liabilities outside the simpler swap design."}]},"synthesis":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","situation":"THORChain continues processing native-asset swaps, with about $12.6 million daily spot volume, but TVL is 94.7 percent below peak and RUNE is 97.9 percent below its high after the THORFi restructuring.","postmortem":"THORFi placed leveraged savings and lending liabilities on top of a reflexive RUNE security model. When RUNE and liquidity weakened, closing loans risked additional minting and pool losses; node operators paused products and converted creditor claims to TCY.","why":"The core swap product solves a real custody and wrapping problem through threshold vaults and unified RUNE liquidity. Expansion into leveraged credit exceeded the resilience of the economic design.","strategic_choices":[{"decision":"Use RUNE as the universal settlement and validator-bond asset.","consequence":"Pool count and routing simplify, but liquidity and security become reflexively tied to RUNE.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://docs.thorchain.org/technical-documentation/understanding-thorchain/rune"]},{"decision":"Custody native assets in rotating threshold-signed vaults.","consequence":"Wrapped assets and centralized custodians are avoided while node and TSS risks become systemic.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://docs.thorchain.org/network-security-governance"]},{"decision":"Expand from swaps into Savers and zero-liquidation Lending.","consequence":"Utility expanded but created approximately $206 million of liabilities and a forced unwind.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://blog.thorchain.org/thorfi-unwind"]}],"lessons_learned":["A useful base exchange can survive failure of an adjacent financial product.","One token serving security, settlement, and collateral creates reflexive tail risk.","Debt restructuring tokens preserve claims but transfer future revenue and complexity."],"could_differ":"Keeping THORChain narrowly focused on swaps would likely have sacrificed lending growth but avoided the THORFi liability overhang and TCY revenue claim.","unknowns":["How much TCY remains unclaimed and how durable is its revenue share?","What is current node and pooled-bond concentration?","Can RUNE security remain overcollateralized during another severe drawdown?","How much volume is organic versus router or affiliate concentration?"],"outlook":{"bull":"Swap demand and app-layer products grow without recreating leverage.","base":"The core exchange survives while TCY claims and weak RUNE economics constrain recovery.","bear":"A vault, connected-chain, or reflexive-security shock triggers another liquidity retreat.","most_likely":"base"},"cause_tags":["native_cross_chain_swaps","threshold_vaults","rune_reflexivity","debt_restructuring"],"confidence":"high"}},"meta":{"dimension_completeness_pct":100,"data_completeness_pct":84,"confidence":"high","unsourced_fields":["team.founders","capital.total_raised_usd","capital.treasury_usd","onchain.stablecoin_tvl_usd","onchain.revenue_30d_usd","onchain.active_addresses_daily","onchain.dev_activity_monthly","onchain.tvl_concentration"],"last_reviewed":"2026-07-29"}}]')
),
dossiers AS (
  SELECT value AS dossier FROM dossier_seed, json_each(dossier_seed.payload)
),
dimension_rows AS (
  SELECT
    json_extract(dossier, '$.chain') AS chain,
    dimensions.key AS dimension,
    dimensions.value AS data,
    (SELECT json_group_array(json(json_extract(dossier, '$.source_catalog.' || source_keys.value)))
     FROM json_each(json_extract(dossier, '$.dimension_sources.' || dimensions.key)) AS source_keys) AS sources
  FROM dossiers, json_each(json_extract(dossier, '$.dimensions')) AS dimensions
),
meta_rows AS (
  SELECT
    json_extract(dossier, '$.chain') AS chain,
    '_meta' AS dimension,
    json_extract(dossier, '$.meta') AS data,
    (SELECT json_group_array(json(value))
     FROM json_each(json_extract(dossier, '$.source_catalog'))) AS sources
  FROM dossiers
)
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO chain_facts (chain, dimension, data, sources, updated_at)
SELECT chain, dimension, data, sources, '2026-07-29' FROM dimension_rows
UNION ALL
SELECT chain, dimension, data, sources, '2026-07-29' FROM meta_rows;
